JetBrains Mono (vendored)

* What

  JetBrains Mono Regular, the canonical monospace TTF from JetBrains.
  Upstream at https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono. SIL OFL
  1.1 — see LICENSE.

* Why this and not Cozette

  We started with Cozette (6x13 bitmap, MIT). Two problems hit us:
    - Cozette ships .bdf only; we converted to .pcf via bdftopcf.
      mlterm's font-fb path renders the resulting PCF with each
      glyph row drawn twice into the descender area, garbling all
      output. Same garbage on every PCF size; not a metrics tweak
      issue, looks like a real upstream mlterm bug specific to how
      bdftopcf-produced PCFs lay out.
    - Cozette's .otb (the OpenType-bitmap variant) is a TrueType
      file with a BDF table inside. mlterm's font-fb path silently
      rejects .otb. Even renaming to .ttf doesn't help; mlterm's
      load path validates the inner tables and bails.

  JetBrains Mono is a real .ttf, renders through mlterm's freetype
  path which works correctly. Modern monospace look (less "pixel"
  than Cozette but still clean), 270 KiB, MIT-equivalent license,
  ubiquitous in editors so no surprises in glyph coverage.

  We can revisit Cozette if either of the mlterm bugs gets fixed
  upstream, or if we figure out a BDF→TTF outline conversion that
  preserves the pixel look (fontforge's autotrace path is slow and
  produces ugly outlines).

* What's here

  JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf  — runtime artefact, what mlterm loads
  LICENSE                    — upstream SIL OFL 1.1, unmodified

* Pinned version

  Master HEAD as of 2026-04-28. JetBrains tags releases on Mono
  with a date scheme; if pinning matters later we can pick a tag
  and document it here.

* How to update

    cd vendor/jetbrains-mono
    curl -sL -o JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf \
      https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono/raw/master/fonts/ttf/JetBrainsMono-Regular.ttf
    curl -sL -o LICENSE \
      https://raw.githubusercontent.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono/master/OFL.txt
